{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>I hated</b> — He mentioned going and walking about, and afterward sitting; \"I did not sit\" and afterward he brought \"I will not enter.\" And the correct interpretation in my eyes: the sense is \"I will not enter their assembly,\" and he mentioned another time, \"and with the wicked I will not sit,\" for men of worthlessness are so in speech, and the wicked in deed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:37.074746749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}